readme.text:
- Four groups ship ready (`cua-screen` / `cua-input` / `browser-heavy` / `vision-heavy`), and they collapse by recent use;
- A collapsed tool **comes back the moment you call it** (a guard catches the call and reopens it) — you never need to know which group it belongs to;
- When a capability is needed the model calls `lazy_tools_enable`; a guard also reopens the **single called tool** (not the whole group) before rejecting it;
- To look around: `lazy_tools_status`; to open everything for this session: `lazy_tools_mode { idleDays: 0 }`.

- Split on `__` or `_`; **descend only when child families cover ≥80%** of the parent, otherwise keep
  the whole family (`mnemon`'s 17 tools are not split into two groups of 3);
- A prefix needs ≥ `minTools` (default 3) tools;
- Prefixes already ≥80% covered by existing groups are skipped;
- **Core tools are never grouped** (`read`, `write`, `edit`, `pwsh`, `grep`, `glob`, `skill`,
  `todo_write`, `lazy_tools_*` …);
- Computed once at session start and frozen for the session (never breaks the prefix cache);
- Auto groups are prefixed `auto-`, visible in `lazy_tools_status`, and removable with
  `lazy_tools_disable auto-xxx`.

```json
{
  "managedRoles": {
    "dsh-superagent-worker": { "allowGroups": ["cua-screen", "browser-heavy"] },
    "subagent": { "allowGroups": ["*"] }

- mounted = tools visible to that session ∪ tools this plugin itself collapsed; only groups with at least one member are listed;
- **if nothing is mounted the whole section disappears** (the host drops empty sections) — no more advertising a group this session cannot reach;
- tools blocked by another layer (a host permission gate, another plugin's deny) are **not** advertised;
- the "N tools are ungrouped, go group them" nudge only appears in default-preset human sessions;
- when the calling session cannot be resolved, the 0.17.x behavior (list every group) is kept — the failure direction is "unchanged", never "shorter".
